&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand the service platform’s asynchronous execution capabilities and make asynchronous systems easy to build, resilient, and scalable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve productivity of the engineers using our systems and work towards ensuring a thoroughly considered developer experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a team of technically sophisticated engineers to solve problems for fellow Stripe engineers by understanding their needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use both qualitative and quantitative metrics to determine priorities and measure effectiveness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver practical, useful, and reliable tools, processes, and code refactorings to Stripe engineers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build client SDKs for developers all over Stripe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve, deploy, scale, and manage services and databases.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to open source frameworks such as Temporal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field, plus two (2) years of related work experience in Software Development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have two (2) years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software Design;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software testing and debugging;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Object Oriented Design (OOD); and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python, C++, Go, Ruby, or Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have six (6) months of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed Systems, including Temporal or Cadence; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure design and large scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $156,800 - $235,200/yr&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. &lt;strong&gt;WA83&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
